This skill adds workspace content to the Coder Nexus `grilling` process, `gate-review` spec mode and `requirements.md` template. Their gates, laws and sections stay as they are.

## Always

- Use the glossary terms of the domain skill verbatim; a synonym is a defect. Add a missing term there before using it.
- Ask only questions that serve a confirmed goal; one question at a time, recommendation first.
- Check every mandatory edge-case category ([03]({{ref_03}})) against the item; record "not applicable" with the reason.
- Write AC as observable behavior that QA can test, with no vague words; write success signals that can be measured ([04]({{ref_04}})).
- For a change, classify each affected BR and AC as ADDED / MODIFIED / REMOVED against the built code ([04]({{ref_04}})).
- Present Gate 1 only after the review questions find nothing open ([05]({{ref_05}})).

Documents for the user are written in {{team_language}}; code names stay as in code.

